title: Women's Rights
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
view-if: spd_in_government = 1 and womens_rights_timer = 0 and chancellor_party == "SPD"
on-arrival: womens_rights_timer += 10; month_actions += 1
card-image: img/portraits/campoamor.jpg
frequency: 50
max-visits: 6

= Women's Rights

According to the 1931 Constitution, women are equal to men under the law, but the patriarchal societal traditions remain a obstacle. continue to face unequal wages and are frequently pressure to abandon their jobs upon marriage. Domestic and civil codes still favor male authority in many aspects of daily life, backed by a deeply reactionary catholic culture.

The left stands mostly united on advancing civil equality, though internal debates persist over the pace of reform.

- @labor: Institute policies that help women in the workforce.
- @family: Reform marriage, divorce, and property law.
- @welfare: Improve welfare for single mothers and children.
- @liberalize: Attempt to liberalize abortion laws.
- @return: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@labor
subtitle: Paid maternal leave policies, equal pay policies, protection against discrimination at the workplace and so on.
on-arrival: womens_work += 1; womens_rights += 1; workers_psoe -= 4 if unemployed > 15; middle_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 4*(1 - dissent); economic_growth += 0.1;
max-visits: 3

These policies boost our standing among urban, working women and educated professionals. [? if unemployed > 15 : However, rising unemployment causes resentment among traditional male workers who view female employment as unwanted competition that lowers their working conditions. ?]

@family
subtitle: Enact comprehensive divorce laws and dismantle traditional patriarchial civil codes.
on-arrival: family_law += 1; womens_rights += 1; middle_psoe += 4*(1-dissent); workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); rural_psoe += 2; catholics_psoe -= 4; polarization += 5;
max-visits: 2

We've enacted legislation legalizing civil divorce and granting women equal standing in marriage. While progressive sectors applaud the change, conservative and catholic groups accuse us of destroying the traditional Spanish family.


@welfare
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget > 0
on-arrival: welfare += 1; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); unemployed_psoe += 5*(1-dissent); budget -= 1; womens_rights += 1; unemployed -= 0.4; inflation += 0.2; economic_growth += 0.3;

We've expanded public funding for maternity assistance and child welfare programs.

@liberalize
max-visits: 1
subtitle: [? if popular_front < 50 : This is unlikely to succeed; we do not have majority support. ?]
go-to: liberalize_fail if popular_front < 50; liberalize_success if popular_front >= 50 and year >= 1934

@liberalize_fail
on-arrival: dlr_relation -= 5; prr_relation -= 5; coalition_dissent += 1; workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); catholics_psoe -= 5;

Unfortunately, our proposal for legalizing abortion has been turned down in the Cortes. Moderate and Catholic-leaning deputies join conservative parties in voting it down, while several conservative members of our own coalition express fierce outrage..

@liberalize_success
on-arrival: abortion_rights += 1; womens_rights += 1; coalition_dissent += 1; dlr_relation -= 8; catholics_psoe -= 10; prr_relation -= 5; workers_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); middle_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); workers_ap += 3; middle_ap += 3; middle_re += 3; rural_psoe += 3; unemployed_psoe += 3*(1-dissent); polarization += 10;

With the backing of a progressive majority in the Cortes, we pass groundbreaking legislation legalizing abortion! This victory solidifies our standing among radical progressives and feminists, but it sparks widespread outrage among catholic conservatives and right-wing organizations, further polarizing the political landscape.
